 "summary": "The PR reuses Mathlib's SeparationQuotient metric machinery rather than hand-rolling a setoid quotient, moves `abs_homDensity_sub_le_cutDist` into Counting.lean instead of duplicating it, and derives all quotient-level bounds from the existing strict-graphon lemmas. The two graphon-facing quotient lemmas are not reachable from the simp set (neither `SeparationQuotient.dist_mk` nor `Metric.inseparable_iff` is `@[simp]`) and are roadmap-pinned, so they are legitimate specializations, not duplication.",
